  "overview": {
    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Ben Allen is a Democratic state senator who was elected in 2014 and represents a district hit by the Los Angeles County fires. He previously served on the Santa Monica-Malibu Board of Education. He has chaired the Senate Environmental Quality Committee and the Budget Subcommittee on Resources, Environmental Protection and Energy.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Ben Allen is a Democratic state senator who was elected in 2014 and represents a district hit by the Los Angeles County fires.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He previously served on the Santa Monica-Malibu Board of Education.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "He has chaired the Senate Environmental Quality Committee and the Budget Subcommittee on Resources, Environmental Protection and Energy.",
            "cites": [3]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He wants to keep insurers in the market by allowing faster rate reviews and forward-looking tools, with guardrails such as requiring them to serve high-risk communities. He would increase staff to handle customer service and create a consumer advocate position in the department. He calls for requiring insurers to explain claim denials and to report delays and outstanding claims after a disaster. He supports restricting new construction in high-risk zones. He wants to reduce risk by bringing together insurers, builders, local governments, firefighters and the state.",
        "cites": [2, 4, 5, 6],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "He wants to keep insurers in the market by allowing faster rate reviews and forward-looking tools, with guardrails such as requiring them to serve high-risk communities.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "He would increase staff to handle customer service and create a consumer advocate position in the department.",
            "cites": [4]
          },
          {
            "text": "He calls for requiring insurers to explain claim denials and to report delays and outstanding claims after a disaster.",
            "cites": [5]
          },
          {
            "text": "He supports restricting new construction in high-risk zones.",
            "cites": [6]
          },
          {
            "text": "He wants to reduce risk by bringing together insurers, builders, local governments, firefighters and the state.",
            "cites": [6]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "As a legislator, Allen authored a law restricting single-use plastics and touts writing Proposition 4, a climate bond measure approved by voters in 2024. He authored Senate Bill 1209, which allows the insurance commissioner to order insurers to fix issues found during investigations without going through a lengthy legal process. He also wrote a law requiring insurers to pay 60% of a policyholder's contents coverage without a detailed inventory. Another law he authored requires insurers to provide more details when planning to drop coverage and gives homeowners time to fix the issues.",
        "cites": [1, 7, 4, 8],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "As a legislator, Allen authored a law restricting single-use plastics and touts writing Proposition 4, a climate bond measure approved by voters in 2024.",
